    "answer_seconds": 1.9422699379938422,
    "total_seconds": 3.036850320000667,
    "answer": "HTTP 429 means the rate limit has been exceeded. The response includes a Retry-After header indicating how many seconds to wait before retrying. You should implement exponential backoff with jitter for retry logic and avoid immediate retries on 429 errors (RATE LIMITING).\n\nThe OAuth access token is valid for 3600 seconds (1 hour). Use the refresh token to obtain a new access token before it expires (API AUTHENTICATION).",
