    "id": "EQ2-07",
    "question": "What protections apply to a privileged administrator who works remotely?",
    "top_score": 0.41720762495714286,
    "top_vector_score": 0.534786403,
    "top_keyword_score": 0.14285714285714285,
    "top_section": "REMOTE WORK POLICY",
    "retrieval_seconds": 0.3007102599949576,
    "answer_seconds": 3.473615126000368,
    "total_seconds": 3.774388532008743,
    "answer": "A privileged administrator working remotely must comply with the following protections:\n\n- Remote work rules: They may work remotely up to 3 days per week after 6 months probation, with manager approval, must maintain a safe workspace, be reachable via Slack during core hours (10 AM\u20133 PM local time), and respond within 30 minutes (REMOTE WORK POLICY).\n- Access control: Their privileged access requires Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA), follows least privilege principles, is reviewed quarterly, and must be individual and auditable (INFORMATION SECURITY POLICY).\n- Encryption: Their laptop must have full-disk encryption enabled (BitLocker or FileVault), and all data in transit must use TLS 1.2 or higher (INFORMATION SECURITY POLICY).\n- Acceptable use: They must not circumvent security controls or expose ACME systems to security risks (ACCEPTABLE USE POLICY).\n\nNo additional specific protections for privileged administrators working remotely are stated beyond these policies.",
