    "retrieval_seconds": 0.3534052269969834,
    "answer_seconds": 2.045301638994715,
    "total_seconds": 2.398734072994557,
    "answer": "For Tier 1 systems, the difference between RTO and RPO is:\n\n- RTO (Recovery Time Objective) is 4 hours, meaning the maximum acceptable downtime before the system must be restored.\n- RPO (Recovery Point Objective) is 1 hour, meaning the maximum acceptable data loss measured in time before recovery.\n\nSo, RTO focuses on how quickly the system must be back online, while RPO focuses on how much data loss is tolerable.",
